    "result_text": "All green \u2014 build succeeds and the acceptance test passes. The audit line confirms the behavior end-to-end: `memberId=V2NSW27...` and `{\"seq\":1,\"schemaVersion\":2,...}`.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** (each a single-line mix-in of a fixed `V2` tag, so every identifier changes and no v1 value recurs):\n- `mapper/HouseholdId.java` \u2014 hashes `\"V2|\" + lastName + \"|\" + postcode`.\n- `mapper/IdentityKey.java` \u2014 hashes `\"V2|\" + telephone + \"|\" + email + \"|\" + soundex`.\n- `rest/function/owner/AssignCustomerCode.java` \u2014 the region code *inside* the memberId becomes `\"V2\" + Locality.of(...)`, so the whole `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` changes.\n\n**User-facing region stays plain** \u2014 `Locality`, `Timezone`, and `OwnerSegment` are untouched, so `locality` is still `NSW`, `timezone` is unchanged, and the owner segment's derived region (`dto.getLocality()`) never carries the `V2` tag.\n\n**Response shape:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added an `OwnerIdentity` schema (`memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey`), replaced the three top-level identity fields with a nested `identity` ref, and added a top-level integer `apiVersion`.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 removed the three now-invalid top-level `@Mapping` lines.\n- `mapper/MembershipDecorator.java` \u2014 sets `apiVersion=2` and builds the nested `identity` (memberId from the V2 customer code, plus V2 householdId/identityKey) in the existing `@AfterMapping` step.\n\n**Audit:**\n- `rest/function/owner/SaveOwner.java` \u2014 the event moves to schema version 2 with an added `\"schemaVersion\":2`; its memberId is the recomputed V2 identity.\n\nStructural impact stayed low: the identity algorithms and the audit event were each one-line edits in small single-method classes, the mapper only lost lines, and the only real growth (three setter calls) went into the already-small decorator rather than into the large `OwnerMapper` interface.\n\nRequest fields are unchanged.",
