    "probe_text": "I now have the complete picture. Here is the ordered trace of `POST /api/owners`, as wired in `owners.POST.yml` and implemented by the function classes.\n\n## Gate (before any step)\n\n- **Authorization** \u2014 `authorize: \"hasRole('OWNER_ADMIN')\"`. Caller must hold `OWNER_ADMIN` or the request is denied.\n\n## Pipeline steps, in order\n\n**1. `RouteIdempotentCreate`** \u2014 reads the optional `Idempotency-Key` header.\n- *Side-effect / branch:* if the key was seen before **and** its owner still exists, publishes that owner and short-circuits to `RespondWithOwner` (**200**, no creation). Otherwise publishes the key (or `\"\"`) for later recording and proceeds to create.\n\n**2. `RequireOwnerFields`** \u2014 reads `@RequestBody`, the one body binding in the pipeline.\n- *Validation:* rejects missing/blank `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone`, and address (needs either a non-blank `addressLine1` or flat `address`). Missing ones are collected \u2192 `MissingOwnerFieldsException` (**400**). Publishes the body as a variable for later steps.\n\n**3. `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`**\n- *Side-effect:* rewrites telephone to E.164 (strips non-digits; keeps `+`/country code, else assumes `+61` and drops a leading `0`).\n- *Validation:* 8\u201315 digits after `+`, and per-country national length (`+61`\u21929, `+1`\u219210); otherwise **400**.\n\n**4. `NormalizeOwnerEmail`**\n- *Side-effect:* if an email is present, lower-cases it.\n- *Validation:* if present, must match the email regex, else **400**. Absent/blank is allowed.\n\n**5. `RejectDisposableEmailDomain`**\n- *Validation:* rejects emails whose domain is on the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 **400**.\n\n**6. `NormalizeOwnerAddress`**\n- *Side-effect:* canonicalizes the address (trim, collapse whitespace, upper-case, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). Prefers structured `addressLine1`/`addressLine2`, composing them into `address`; else normalizes flat `address` in place.\n\n**7. `RejectDuplicateOwnerIdentity`**\n- *Validation:* scans all non-deleted owners; if the `IdentityKey` (normalized telephone + email + lastName) matches an existing one \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` (**409**).\n\n**8. `RejectCrowdedCity`**\n- *Validation:* if the city already holds \u226550 owners (case-insensitive) \u2192 `CrowdedCityException` (**409**).\n\n**9. `RejectDailyLimit`**\n- *Validation:* if \u2265100 owners already registered on the current business day \u2192 `DailyLimitException` (**429**).\n\n**10. `RejectInvalidPostcode`**\n- *Validation:* postcode is optional; if present it must be 4 digits and, for a known region (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099), fall in range \u2192 `InvalidPostcodeException` (**400**).\n\n**11. `RejectFutureRegistrationDate`**\n- *Validation:* if a supplied `registrationDate` is after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (**400**). Absent date is allowed.\n\n**12. `BuildOwner`** *(transaction begins here; steps 12\u201317 all `govern: [ transaction ]`)*\n- *Validation:* `@Valid` on the DTO triggers the bean-validation constraints now \u2014 `firstName`/`lastName` `@NotNull @Pattern @Size(1..30)`, `city` `@NotNull @Size(1..80)`, `telephone` `@NotNull @Pattern(^[0-9]*$) @Size(1..20)`, `postcode` `@Pattern(^[0-9]{4}$)`, `title` `@Size(max 10)`, address fields `@Size`, etc. (violations \u2192 `MethodArgumentNotValidException`, **400**).\n- *Side-effect:* maps DTO \u2192 `Owner`; sets `registrationDate` (defaults to today) rolled forward to the next business day via `BusinessDay.onOrAfter`.\n\n**13. `AssignCustomerCode`**\n- *Side-effect:* computes and sets `customerCode` = `<region><FY2><HASH8><checkDigit>` (region from postcode/city, two-digit fiscal year, first 8 hex of SHA-256 of telephone+lastName, Luhn check digit). Pure function, no repo lookup.\n\n**14. `DeduplicateCustomerCode`**\n- *Side-effect:* if the code collides with an existing owner's, appends `-<n>` (smallest n\u22652) to make it unique.\n\n**15. `CountNamesakes`**\n- *Side-effect:* sets `namesakeCount` = number of pre-existing owners with the same first+last name (case-insensitive).\n\n**16. `DetectPossibleDuplicate`**\n- *Side-effect:* sets `possibleDuplicate`/`possibleDuplicateOf`. Skipped (stays false) if `sharesHousehold` is true; otherwise flags true when an existing owner has a different identity key but matching `soundex(lastName)` **and** postcode.\n\n**17. `SaveOwner`**\n- *Side-effect:* persists via `ownerRepository.save(owner)`; then computes a membership level and emits **audit logs** (`AUDIT` logger: a human line and a versioned JSON event with an incrementing sequence) and a **welcome notification** (`NOTIFY` logger).\n\n**18. `RecordIdempotencyKey`** *(transaction)*\n- *Side-effect:* if an `Idempotency-Key` was supplied, records `key \u2192 owner.id` in the `IdempotencyStore` so a later repeat returns this owner.\n\n**19. `RespondWithOwnerCreated`** *(transaction)*\n- *Side-effect:* maps to `OwnerDto`, sets `bulkSignupWarning` (true when >80 owners registered on the current business day), and responds **201 Created** with `Location: /api/owners/{id}`. Transaction commits at the end of the pipeline.\n\n---\n\nOne thing worth flagging (you asked me only to read, so I've changed nothing): step 3 rewrites `telephone` to a leading-`+` E.164 string, but the bean-validation `@Pattern(regexp = \"^[0-9]*$\")` on `telephone` that runs at step 12 (`BuildOwner`'s `@Valid`) only permits digits \u2014 so a normalized telephone appears to violate its own constraint. That looks like a latent inconsistency rather than intended behavior; let me know if you'd like me to dig into whether it actually trips at runtime."
